      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T22:18:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. And no, nothing needs to be copied. hash_table_reserve() is called after the count pass, and the fill then writes every entry of that block size from scratch. Each block size is built once per frame, so no old entry is ever read. If the allocation fails, the array is NULL with size 0, and the caller reports AOM_CODEC_MEM_ERROR.",
      "parentUuid": "0e5ab6d0_a222120b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "1f64de19a06ab90dccc7b9c96ee2ff3710383d75",
